###############################################################################
# Reference FX: NBP and ECB official fixings through the provider boundary,
# and the reporting-currency resolver.
#
# It covers the official-source ops surface, reference board rows with both
# clocks and raw provenance, the provider-filtered stream, a keyless table
# refresh, the FX resolver with full provenance, the NBP-vs-ECB cross-check,
# and the guards that keep reference rows out of the tradeable universe.
#
# Prerequisites: the full stack is running. NBP and ECB need no API key.
# Fixings publish on business days (NBP ~12:15, ECB ~16:00 CET); on a weekend
# every row carries Friday's as-of date and still classifies as current.
###############################################################################

@marketData = http://localhost:8001
@actions    = http://localhost:8008
@books      = http://localhost:8004

# ========================= OFFICIAL-SOURCE RUNTIME =========================

### Both official sources are wired: keyless, calendar-window strategy, last as-of
GET {{marketData}}/providers

### One official source in detail — no invented budget, a publication schedule instead
GET {{marketData}}/providers/NBP/health

# ========================= REFERENCE BOARD ROWS ============================

### Reference rows carry grade REFERENCE, basis REFERENCE_MID, the as-of as
### provider time, a fresh received time, and origin reference=true
GET {{marketData}}/market-data/quotes?provider=NBP

###
GET {{marketData}}/market-data/quotes?provider=ECB

### One fixing pair via the canonical detail route
GET {{marketData}}/market-data/quotes/NBP/EURPLN

### The EUR/PLN cross-check pair: NBP vs ECB publish independent fixings —
### compare the two mids; the UI chip shows the difference in bps
GET {{marketData}}/market-data/quotes?symbol=EURPLN

### Gold is PLN per 1 gram (XAUPLN_G), never merged with per-ounce XAU pairs
GET {{marketData}}/market-data/quotes/NBP/XAUPLN_G

### Fixing history with the raw source table behind every stored observation
GET {{marketData}}/market-data/quotes/NBP/EURPLN/history?limit=10&raw=1

# ========================= STREAM AND TABLE REFRESH ========================

### Run separately: the NBP-filtered stream stays open and only emits NBP events
GET {{marketData}}/market-data/stream/NBP

### Keyless table refresh — refetches table A + gold and republishes every row
POST {{marketData}}/market-data/refresh?provider=NBP

###
POST {{marketData}}/market-data/refresh?provider=ECB

# ============================ THE FX RESOLVER ==============================

### Every resolvable currency to PLN, each with rate, path, provider and as-of
GET {{marketData}}/fx/rates?to=PLN

### To USD: EUR→USD is a direct ECB rate; PLN→USD inverts NBP's USD/PLN fixing
GET {{marketData}}/fx/rates?to=USD

### An unpublished target: every row answers with an honest no-path reason
GET {{marketData}}/fx/rates?to=GBP

### Not a currency code
GET {{marketData}}/fx/rates?to=ZLOTY

# ======================= REFERENCE ROWS NEVER TRADE ========================

### The tradeable universe derives from watched ∪ held only — no NBP/ECB rows
GET {{actions}}/instruments

### Watch EURPLN on a quote provider: the same symbol now has one tradeable
### TWELVE_DATA row next to the two official fixing rows
POST {{marketData}}/watchlist
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "EURPLN", "asset_class": "FX", "currency": "PLN", "providers": ["TWELVE_DATA"] }

### Three EURPLN rows: one REALTIME quote, two REFERENCE fixings
GET {{marketData}}/market-data/quotes?symbol=EURPLN

### A real FX book, so the forged intent below fails on the provider, not the book
# @name fxBook
POST {{books}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "REFERENCE_GUARD_{{$timestamp}}", "expected_asset_class": "FX" }

###
@fxBookId = {{fxBook.response.body.$.book_id}}

### A forged NBP intent is refused with the reason (422)
POST {{actions}}/trade-actions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "client_request_id": "forged-nbp-{{$timestamp}}", "book_id": "{{fxBookId}}", "asset_class": "FX", "symbol": "EURPLN", "side": "BUY", "quantity": 1000, "market_data_provider": "NBP", "client_seen_price": "4.31" }

### NBP cannot be added to the watchlist — reference data is system-owned (400)
POST {{marketData}}/watchlist
Content-Type: application/json

{ "symbol": "EURPLN", "asset_class": "FX", "currency": "PLN", "providers": ["NBP"] }

### Cleanup: deactivate the guard book, drop the EURPLN quote membership
DELETE {{books}}/books/{{fxBookId}}

###
DELETE {{marketData}}/watchlist/EURPLN?provider=TWELVE_DATA
